  <p class="answer">Jeff Richardson is the Owner of {entity.name}, a Boise, Idaho company formed to buy one established Treasure Valley business. He holds an MBA from Northwestern's Kellogg School of Management, worked in financial analytics at ServiceLink, a Fidelity National Financial company, and did strategy consulting at EY. He has spent several years studying Treasure Valley businesses.</p>

<h2>Who is Jeff Richardson?</h2>
<p>I am Jeffrey (Jeff) Richardson, Owner of {entity.name} I live in Boise, Idaho, and the company exists for one reason: to buy one good, established business in the Treasure Valley and own it for a long time.</p>
<p>Before this, I worked in financial analytics at ServiceLink, a Fidelity National Financial (FNF) company, and in strategy consulting at EY. I hold an MBA from the Kellogg School of Management at Northwestern University. The short version is that I have spent my career reading businesses through their numbers and helping the people who run them make decisions. I can tell the difference between a good business with messy books and a messy business with good marketing, and I do not need a broker's packet to see the value in a company that has quietly done well for a long time.</p>
